{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"misandrous-rockable-hornbill","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nF01 introduced a documentation policy that bans U+003B and U+2014 in ticket writing. The deterministic close guard requires both code points in every `[non-codebase]` provenance declaration. F01 cannot close while satisfying both contracts.\n\n## Current enforcement\n\nThe parser reads only the first indented `provenance` continuation. It splits fields only on U+003B and extracts the required justification only after U+2014. The close precheck promotes parser failures to blocking status before completion verification. No punctuation-compliant syntax is accepted.\n\n## Historical basis\n\nADR 0061 pins the single-line grammar and states that the deterministic layer does not block. Ticket binary-cobwebby-bittern later promoted the parser to blocking close behavior without an accepted ADR amendment. ADR 0101 changes the canonical acceptance criterion tag and states that ADR 0061 remains unaffected.\n\n## Proposed direction\n\nAdopt a backward-compatible multiline grammar.\n\n```text\nprovenance:\n  environment = <value>\n  principal = <value>\n  privilege_posture = <value>\n  instrument = <value>\n  justification = <text>\n```\n\nContinue accepting the legacy grammar for historical records. Update the parser, close diagnostic, author guidance, plan-review lint, and tests to emit and accept the multiline form. Preserve deterministic provenance completeness and anti-laundering enforcement. Record the contract change through an ADR that amends or supersedes the relevant part of ADR 0061.\n\n## Alternatives\n\nRestoring advisory or grandfathered close behavior would weaken the close defense added by binary-cobwebby-bittern. Rewriting command outcomes as repository facts would misclassify their evidence. Adding legacy declarations would violate the F01 policy. A forced close would bypass signed completion verification.\n\n## Decision status\n\nPending operator approval. Do not implement this ticket or write an ADR until approved.","id":"c2ec-10b0-4bd9-430d","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","architecture","gates"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Support punctuation-compliant measurement provenance"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787348248732686001,"uuid":"685ecd2d-54c2-4e56-97be-519fbc95b25e"}